SUMMARY:Pensacola Archaeological Society Lecture: Early Spanish Florida
LOCATION:Florida Public Archaeology Network Coordinating Center\, 207 E Mai
 n St\, Pensacola\, FL 32502
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday 10/13 · 7:00 PM to 8:00 PM\n\nThe University of West F
 lorida's president emerita gives an overview of the first 250 years of the
  Spanish colony of Florida\, from 1513 to 1763. The talk covers Spain's sh
 ifting strategies to hold the Atlantic coast and protect the gold fleets s
 ailing from Cuba to Spain. The lecture meets downtown at the Florida Publi
 c Archaeology Network's Coordinating Center\, and no pre-registration is r
 equired.\n\nPrice: No published price\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures
 .com/events/ev-pensacola-archaeological-society-lecture-early-spanish-flor
 ida-1013.html
